ll Terminals hand (unlikely).  \n\nBetter discard is **T9**: terminal, only 3 left, but we have 1 in hand. Others have melded terminals? Across has T2 T3 T4, not terminal chow; next has T3 T4 T5 and T7 T8 T9 (terminal chow 789), so they already completed a T7 T8 T9 chow, so T9 is safe for next player. Previous has W2 W3 W4 no terminal. So T9 relatively safe.  \n\nT6 we have 3 of \u2014 if we keep T6\u00d73, we can pung if drawn 4th, or use as pair if needed. But keeping 3 of same tile blocks others from pung.  \n\nBest discard for offense: We want to keep tiles that can form chows: W3 W6 could form with W4 W5, but W6 alone not useful without W4 W5 or W5 W7. W9 not useful except with W7 W8.  \n\nActually keep T2, T8, T9 to possibly make bamboo chows: T2 with T1 T3 or T3 T4; T8 with T7 T9 or T6 T7; T9 with T7 T8 (but T8 is ours, T7 unseen 3).  \n\nI think discard **W9** is okay: It\u2019s isolated, terminal, not connecting to others in hand.  \n\nBut among options given: Play T9, T6, W9, J1, T8, W3, T2, W6.  \n\n**Evaluation**:  \n1. Play J1 \u2014 discarding honor reduces chance for dragon pung but avoids giving someone pung of J1.  \n2. Play W9 \u2014 discard terminal, but keeps bamboo suit concentration for possible half flush later.  \n3. Play T9 \u2014 discard terminal bamboo, but we keep T8 maybe for T7 T8 T9 chow if we draw T7.  \n\nBut T7 unseen 3, possible to draw. If we keep T8 T9 and draw T7, that\u2019s a chow. If we discard T9, we lose that. So maybe keep T9.  \n\nBetter: discard W9 or W3 or W6 to reduce suits, aiming for Half Flush with bamboo + honors. Our honors only J1, maybe get wind tile later.  \n\nGiven we have T6\u00d73 already, could aim for All Pungs pattern (6 pts) if we make other melds pungs. To do that, need more duplicates. Keep J1\u00d72, try to get third J1, and make other pungs.  \n\nThus discard a suited lone tile: W3, W6, or W9.  \n\nW3 has 3 left unseen, someone may chow W1 W2 W3 or W2 W3 W4 \u2014 but previous player melded W2 W3 W4, so W3 not needed by them.  \n\nI think safest: W9 (terminal, less dangerous because others not collecting terminals evidently).  \n\n**Reason**:  \nW9 is a terminal with 3 left unseen, not connected to other tiles in hand, unlikely to complete a chow for opponents given game history, and discarding it simplifies hand towards possible half-flush in bamboo or keeping T6 triplet for pung-based hand.  \n\n**Answer**: Play W9"}
